  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure will maintain fair weather and \na gradual warming trend through Saturday.\n\nCoastal low pressure maturing off the New England coast late this \nweek and into the weekend will cause surface high pressure centered \nover eastern Canada to gradually settle south across the region \nFriday before further pushing westward across the central Great \nLakes by Saturday. Overall fair weather will persist through the end \nof the work week and into the start of the weekend. \n\nClear skies and light winds tonight will be favorable for \nradiational cooling, and result in another cool night. Temperatures \nin the mid to upper 30s are likely across the Tug Hill region, and \nlow to mid 40s are expected across the lower elevations. Otherwise, \nsome patchy fog may develop across the river valleys.",
